course: dictionary
lesson: 6378
title: Pictures and their stories
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A picture can show a face, but it does not always show the whole story. Read the words around the word mugshot to find its meaning. The clues tell you when it is used and what it means.
explain: «The news showed a mugshot of the man before his court case.» The clues are news and court case. A mugshot is a photo the police take of someone after an arrest. Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence: a police photo of a face fits.
explain: Be careful: a mugshot shows that someone was arrested, not that they are guilty. Ask what happened before and after the picture. Jokingly, people also call passport photos or school ID pictures mugshots.
fact: A mugshot is a photograph of a person's face, taken from the front and the side.
fact: The police take mugshots after an arrest.
fact: Informally, any photo of someone's face can be called a mugshot, especially an unflattering one.
fact: Common phrases are «police mugshot» and «take a mugshot».
fact: Being in a mugshot means someone was arrested, not that they are guilty.
exercise: «The police took a mugshot of the suspect.» What is a mugshot here? | *A photo of a face, taken by the police after an arrest | A song from a music video | A famous painting | A picture of a dog in a park
exercise: Ella says her school ID picture is a mugshot. What is she doing? | Telling the truth about the police | *Joking, using the informal meaning of any face photo | Describing a visit to the passport office | Painting a picture of her face
exercise: Which sentence shows that a mugshot does not prove guilt? | A mugshot shows a dog in a park | *Someone is shown in a mugshot after an arrest, but the court has not decided yet | Mugshots are always taken from music videos | Anyone in a mugshot must have stolen something
test: Which phrase is used for a police photo of a suspect? | Dinner party | *Police mugshot | Garden gate | Sunny beach
test: What does «a picture without its story can lie» suggest? | Pictures never tell the truth | Only music videos are true | *A photo can look like one thing, but the full story may be different | Stories are always more useful than pictures
exam: The news shows a mugshot and the caption says the man was arrested. What is the safest thing to say? | The photo is from a music video | He is guilty because the police took the photo | The police made a mistake | *He was arrested, and we must wait for the court to decide if he is guilty
